<!-- Horizontal travel of the *folder* page's post-commit back exit.

     Same 96dp contract as the shared page exit
     (DefaultCrossActivityBackAnimation retargets the closing rect to
     currentClosingRect.left + cross_activity_back_entering_start_offset, which is
     96dp). Only the shape differs.

     The shared resource uses fast_out_slow_in, whose slow start is correct for a page
     that fades away on top of a parent that is itself moving in. On the folder branch
     the parent does not move at all, so the foreground has to carry the departure:
     travel is front-loaded, the fastest section coincides with the steep part of
     oxygen_classic_folder_back_alpha, and the tail decelerates into the 96dp endpoint
     on the frame the fade reaches 0 (90% of the 220 ms clock, i.e. 0.968 of the travel).

     Measured travel fractions (same AnimationSet#getTransformationAt path):
         progress   fast_out_slow_in   this curve
         0.02       0.001             0.014
         0.10       0.026             0.094
         0.20       0.134             0.238
         0.30       0.261             0.403
         0.50       0.500             0.700
         0.80       0.800             0.920
         1.00       1.000             1.000

     PathInterpolator contract: starts at (0,0), ends at (1,1), x strictly
     increasing (0.16 -> 0.28 -> 0.50 -> 0.70 -> 0.87 -> 1). -->
<pathInterpolator xmlns:android="http://schemas.android.com/apk/res/android"
    android:pathData="M0,0 C0.16,0.10 0.28,0.42 0.50,0.70 C0.70,0.88 0.87,0.97 1,1" />
